{"meta":{"dataset":"vehicle-complaints","title":"Vehicle safety complaints by state, make and model year (NHTSA complaint file)","version":"1.0.0","doi":"10.5281/zenodo.23744214","doiUrl":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23744214","conceptDoi":"10.5281/zenodo.23744213","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","attribution":"Source: Probative, Vehicle safety complaints by state, make and model year (NHTSA complaint file), version 1.0.0, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23744214, licensed CC BY 4.0.","citation":"Probative. (2026). Vehicle safety complaints by state, make and model year (NHTSA complaint file) (Version 1.0.0) [Data set]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23744214","disclaimer":"Not legal advice. These are counts of unverified complaints that vehicle owners filed with NHTSA, kept for research and marketing planning. A complaint is not a finding that a vehicle is defective, and a count says nothing about whether any owner has a lemon-law or injury claim. Rights and deadlines are for your own counsel.","notice":"Probative is a marketing firm, not a law firm; not legal advice.","lastChecked":"2026-10-28","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/index.json","humanUrl":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/vehicle-complaints/","statusCodes":{"P":"primary source","S":"secondary source","D":"ABA model default","U":"open question"}},"summary":"Safety complaints about cars, trucks, SUVs, motorcycles and RVs that owners filed with the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA), counted from its Office of Defects Investigation complaint file for the ten most recent model years, by the complainant's state, the make, the model year and the part of the vehicle named (engine, brakes, air bags, steering and the other NHTSA component groups). Each record gives the complaints, how many report a crash, a fire, an injury or a death, the people reported injured and killed, the complaints filed in the last twelve months, and how many concern a make, model and year that has a safety recall (and a recall of the same system), joined from NHTSA's recall file. State records list every make; make records add the model year by component table and each model's counts; national make records add each model by model year and the number of recall campaigns. A complaint is counted once however many parts it names. Only counts are kept: no narrative, VIN, city, name or complaint number.","key":"jurisdiction","count":4040,"keys":[{"key":"AK","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/AK.json","records":42},{"key":"AL","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/AL.json","records":57},{"key":"AR","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/AR.json","records":56},{"key":"AS","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/AS.json","records":7},{"key":"AZ","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/AZ.json","records":91},{"key":"CA","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/CA.json","records":146},{"key":"CO","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/CO.json","records":97},{"key":"CT","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/CT.json","records":59},{"key":"DC","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/DC.json","records":43},{"key":"DE","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/DE.json","records":46},{"key":"FL","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/FL.json","records":135},{"key":"GA","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/GA.json","records":91},{"key":"GU","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/vehicle-complaints/jurisdictions/GU.json","records":11},{"key":"HI","url":"https://probativ